WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.620
In House of the Dragon Episode 9, the king
is dead – and his body is not even cold

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.570
before his family starts fighting for his
throne.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:17.450
This episode focusses on Alicent’s family,
the greens, in their plots to make Aegon king.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.660
So what happens, and what does it mean?

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:25.050
This video has no spoilers for future episodes,
except for some minor background info.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.770
The opening sequence family tree has been
updated.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:34.219
The symbol for King Viserys is now flooded
with blood to show that he’s dead.

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:39.590
The symbol for Alicent Hightower now shows
the Hightower sigil within the star of the

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.520
Faith of the Seven – cause Alicent now wears
that religious symbol.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:47.070
Alicent’s daughter Helaena has a symbol
of a spider, cause Helaena likes bugs, and

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.309
she stitches a spider picture this episode.

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:54.350
Aegon’s symbol looks like a woman and a
dragon egg.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:01:00.030
And Aemond’s symbol is a sapphire – in
the books, Aemond wears a sapphire in his

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.090
empty eye socket.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:07.729
The bloodlines also show that Alicent has
a fourth child who we haven’t seen yet – a

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:10.020
son named Daeron.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.990
The author George Martin said they couldn’t
fit Daeron into this season of Hot D, but

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:20.970
Daeron will appear in Season 2 –for now,
Daeron is in OIdtown serving Lord Hightower

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.850
as cupbearer, so his symbol is a cup.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:30.630
Aegon now has three children with Helaena
– a girl named Jaehaera, and a boy named

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.530
Jaehaerys, and a boy named Maelor.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:40.540
In the books, Jaehaerys has six fingers on
one of his hands, and six toes on each foot,

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:45.159
so Jaehaerys and Jaehaera’s symbols are
six-fingered hands.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:50.390
The first person to discover that King Viserys
is dead is this servant boy.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:55.649
With his blonde hair, he kinda looks like
a Targaryen – this episode reveals that

00:01:55.649 --> 00:02:02.869
Aegon has some bastard children, so we might
wonder if this boy is a secret Targaryen bastard…

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:04.649
Or he’s just blonde.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:08.020
The boy tells Talya that the king is dead.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.509
So Talya tells Queen Alicent.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:16.700
But then Talya lights some candles in a window
as a signal to tell Mysaria that the king

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.959
is dead.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:23.099
Because Talya is a spy for Mysaria, and Mysaria
can use this information to her advantage

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:25.830
by kidnapping Prince Aegon.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.410
Alicent believes that Viserys wanted their
son Aegon to be king.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:36.780
And that’s not true, Alicent misunderstood
Viserys’ words, but she believes this is

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.950
her husband’s dying wish.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:43.790
We see Alicent’s grief for Viserys, this
is deeply personal for her.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:50.360
But at council, Alicent sees that Otto Tyland
and Jasper don’t care about Viserys’ wishes.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:56.540
Cause they were already plotting to crown
Aegon, secretly scheming behind Alicent’s

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.540
back.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:02.610
They plan to make the City Watch loyal to
them, they’ll move the crown’s gold for

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:07.519
safekeeping, they plan alliances with the
Tullys, Tyrells and Baratheons.

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:10.990
And they don’t include Alicent in their
plans.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:16.459
Alicent had thought that as the queen they
respected her enough to include her – but

00:03:16.459 --> 00:03:18.269
apparently not.

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:24.140
Alicent learns that Otto plans to kill Rhaenyra,
so that Rhaenyra can’t challenge Aegon,

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:29.879
and Alicent is outraged – for all her disagreements
with Rhaenyra, she doesn’t want Rhaenyra

00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:30.879
murdered.

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:33.819
She wants to honour her dead husband’s wishes.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:39.819
So Alicent and Otto both want Aegon to be
king, but while Otto is willing to murder,

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.959
Alicent wants a peaceful transition.

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:45.239
And this is a change from the books.

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:50.140
In the books, Alicent doesn’t protect Rhaenyra,
in fact she reportedly hopes that Rhaenyra

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.650
will die in childbirth.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.720
The show makes Alicent more peaceful and sympathetic.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:02.799
The books also include more specific arguments
over the succession, like Otto says they can’t

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:07.180
let Rhaenyra be queen, cause she’s married
to Daemon, and Daemon would be a terrible

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.110
cruel king consort who might kill them all.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:15.330
Jasper says Aegon should be king because of
succession laws that put men before women,

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:21.190
and cause the Harrenhal Council chose the
male Viserys over the female Rhaenys.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.310
While Criston says Rhaenyra should not rule
because she’s a slut who will who will make

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.330
the Red Keep a big slutty brothel.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:33.370
Criston is.. still really butthurt about his
rejection by Rhaenyra.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:38.120
The only one to stand up for Rhaenyra is Lyman
Beesbury.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.550
Lyman often seemed a weak and irrelevant old
man.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:48.630
But he refuses to go along with this coup
– he says Viserys always said that Rhaenyra

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:53.870
was his heir, and they can’t change the
succession based on Alicent’s word that

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.440
he changed his mind on his deathbed.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:02.440
Lyman hints that Viserys may have been murdered
– in the books, Mushroom claims that Alicent

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.310
poisoned Viserys.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.340
Criston is angered by the insult to Alicent.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:13.610
So he slams Lyman down, and Lyman is killed,
with a stone council ball to his head.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:17.820
In the books, there are three different stories
of how Lyman dies.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.630
Eustace says that Criston cut Lyman’s throat.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:25.580
Mushroom says that Criston threw Lyman out
a window.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.410
And Orwyle says that Lyman was just imprisoned,
and then died of a chill.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:37.280
The book Fire &amp; Blood plays with unreliable
narration, rumour and bias twist the truth.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:41.910
Orwyle is one of the historical sources for
this part of the book, and Orwyle sometimes

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:44.580
lies to make himself look good.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:49.759
Harrold says Criston should be removed from
the Kingsguard for murdering Lyman.

00:05:49.759 --> 00:05:52.770
Just as he previously murdered Joffrey Lonmouth.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:57.380
But Alicent protects Criston because he’s
useful to her.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:03.240
The Kingsguard are meant to be a sacred brotherhood
of noble knights – not murderers helping

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.970
to steal the Throne.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:09.520
So Harrold is outraged that the Kingsguard
are being corrupted by politics.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.979
Otto tells Harrold to go and arrest Rhaenyra.

00:06:12.979 --> 00:06:17.630
But Harrold was Rhaenyra’s friend and protector
since she was a kid.

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:20.370
He won’t give her to the greens to be murdered.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:25.840
He doesn’t accept their authority – cause
he’s sworn to serve the king, and there

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.150
is no king.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:33.840
So Harrold removes his cloak and leaves, kinda
like when Barristan leaves in Game of Thrones.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:38.810
Maybe Harrold will turn up again later to
support a different ruler, like Barristan

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:39.810
does.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.360
The greens are ready to make Aegon the new
king.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.180
But Aegon is missing, so Alicent and Otto
race to find him.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:53.449
Alicent hopes that if she finds Aegon first,
she’ll be able to influence Aegon, and make

00:06:53.449 --> 00:06:57.919
sure the succession happens peacefully without
hurting Rhaenyra.

00:06:57.919 --> 00:07:04.870
She could even make Aegon remove Otto as Hand
of the King, or hold Aegon hostage.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:10.310
As Renly says in Game of Thrones, “he who
holds the king holds the kingdom”.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:15.640
In the books, Tyrion and Cersei both try to
capture Tommen for themselves.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:19.620
Sometimes the king is used as a pawn in the
game of thrones.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.500
Otto sends the twins Ser EErryk and Ser AArryk
to find Aegon.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.520
While Alicent sends Criston and Aemond.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:32.860
The teams race across the city searching for
clues to find Aegon – it’s like The Amazing

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:36.250
Race, and the prize is a drunk prince.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:40.710
Alicent tells Helaena and Aemond that their
father Viserys is dead.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:46.720
Alicent tries to comfort Helaena, but she
pulls away – Alicent’s children are difficult

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:47.720
to love.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:52.919
Otto and Alicent want the king’s death to
stay secret until they’re ready to take

00:07:52.919 --> 00:07:53.919
power.

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:57.710
So they round up servants and lords at the
Keep, and lock them up so they can’t blab

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.789
to Rhaenyra.

00:07:58.789 --> 00:08:01.360
Rhaenys is locked in her room.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:05.030
Otto makes the lords swear to support Aegon.

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:09.680
These aren’t, like, all the lords in Westeros,
it’s just the minor lords who happened to

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.960
be in the Red Keep today.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:14.060
Most of them agree to support Aegon.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:17.720
But Lord Merryweather and Lady Fell refuse.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.770
House Merryweather rules Longtable in the
Reach.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.310
And House Fell rules Fellwood in the stormlands.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:28.870
Merryweather and Fell are old enough that
they were probably at the ceremony years ago

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:31.830
when everyone swore to support Rhaenyra as
heir.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:39.279
So they refuse to break their oath by supporting
Aegon, so Otto imprisons these loyalists.

00:08:39.279 --> 00:08:43.930
Lord Allun Caswell wants to support Rhaenyra
– we’ve seen him friendly with Rhaenyra

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:49.720
before – so Allun pretends to support Aegon,
but then he tries to escape the Keep to go

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:55.019
tell Rhaenyra that the greens are stealing
her throne – but Allun is captured, and

00:08:55.019 --> 00:08:57.880
Otto and Larys put Allun to death.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:03.850
Allun is hanged in the Keep courtyard as a
warning to other rebels.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.810
Alicent asks Rhaenys to support her.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:12.579
Rhaenys is effectively in charge of the powerful
House Velaryon, and Rhaenys has the great

00:09:12.579 --> 00:09:13.760
dragon Meleys.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:19.080
So Rhaenys could be a powerful ally for Aegon
and the greens.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:24.510
Alicent says that allying with Rhaenyra and
Daemon has only hurt Rhaenys and her family.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:28.860
Alicent says Rhaenys should have been the
queen of Westeros.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:33.620
But since Rhaenys and Alicent can’t rule
the realm themselves, they should instead

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:38.970
influence King Aegon and the council, gently
guiding the kingdom towards peace.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.890
But Rhaenys says that’s bullshit.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:46.410
She and Alicent don’t have real power when
they’re serving men.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:52.490
Like, Rhaenys told Corlys for years that his
ambitions put their children in danger, but

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:58.029
he didn’t listen and now their children
are dead.

00:09:58.029 --> 00:10:03.870
Alicent is the queen, yet even she doesn’t
have power when it matters – like when the

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:08.660
men take over the succession and plot murder
and war without her.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:14.829
So Rhaenys says that gentle female influence
within this patriarchy is just a window in

00:10:14.829 --> 00:10:21.480
their prison cell, it’s an illusion, and
the only real power is taking the Throne itself.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.730
And that’s what Rhaenyra wants to do.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:28.829
Unlike Alicent, Rhaenyra has always resisted
the rules of sex and gender.

00:10:28.829 --> 00:10:34.740
She wants to be the first woman on the Throne,
she said she’ll create a new order.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.829
Rhaenys doesn’t much believe in Rhaenyra
either.

00:10:38.829 --> 00:10:42.400
She told Rhaenyra that she’ll fail to change
the system.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:47.399
Rhaenys’ actor says that after Rhaenys’
own failure to take the Throne, she almost

00:10:47.399 --> 00:10:53.070
wants to believe that the patriarchy can’t
be touched, that no woman will truly rule

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.070
Westeros.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:59.709
But Rhaenys is impressed by Alicent’s determination
for peace.

00:10:59.709 --> 00:11:06.820
She maybe feels hope as well as cynicism and
resentment, and feels fear that this this

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:10.320
conflict may cause more death.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:12.889
Criston and Aemond search for Aegon.

00:11:12.889 --> 00:11:18.389
Aemond wears a hood and Criston wears a hat,
as though they’re cosplaying Rhaenyra and

00:11:18.389 --> 00:11:20.529
Dameon in Episode 4.

00:11:20.529 --> 00:11:24.750
They go to a brothel that Aemond and Aegon
had visited as teenagers.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:31.070
A woman there recognises Aemond, and he seems
embarrassed – maybe he lost his virginity

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:36.519
with this woman, maybe he feels ashamed, we
don’t know much about Aemond’s sexuality.

00:11:36.519 --> 00:11:38.620
But Aegon isn’t here.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:44.550
So Aemond says Aegon could be captured, or
dead, or on a ship to Yi Ti.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:50.290
Yi Ti is a powerful empire in the far east,
inspired by Imperial China.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:56.650
Corlys Velaryon is one of the few Westerosi
who have been to Yi Ti on his famous voyages.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:12:03.100
HBO is developing an animated spin-off show
about Yi Ti, called The Golden Empire.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:09.290
Aemond is mad that Aegon gets to be king,
when Aegon is an irresponsible asshole.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:14.529
Aemond studies hard and trains so that he
thinks he should be king.

00:12:14.529 --> 00:12:19.339
Aemond says that he is next in line for the
Throne.

00:12:19.339 --> 00:12:25.680
Which is not true – legally, Aegon’s children
are his heirs, before his brother Aemond.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:32.080
Though there is a fan theory that Aemond might
actually be the father of Helaena’s children,

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:35.820
that they have a secret incestuous love affair.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:42.620
There have been several sibling love triangles
in the books, this a classic Targaryen move.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.660
And Aemond has shown interest in Helaena before.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.690
While Aegon mostly ignores Helaena.

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:56.079
And if Aemond was secretly the father of Helaena’s
children, then Aemond would legally be Aegon’s

00:12:56.079 --> 00:12:57.130
heir.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.399
But that’s just a wild theory.

00:12:58.399 --> 00:13:04.430
The point is that Aemond has that jealous
second son syndrome that we’ve seen in Daemon

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.940
and Vaemond, wanting what their older brother
has.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:14.100
Helaena says this episode that it’s human
nature to be envious of what others have – envy

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:18.240
is a big motivation for many characters in
this story.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.860
Criston understands how Aemond feels.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:27.260
Because Criston is a lower-class person who’s
had to work harder for his status on the Kingsguard

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:30.750
compared to the rich privileged sons of lords.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:36.949
Criston resents Rhaenyra for her privilege,
he once called her a spoiled c-word – which

00:13:36.949 --> 00:13:41.860
is funny, cause in this episode he says that
all women should be respected.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:48.800
Criston is both chivalrous, and misogynistic
– he uses his image as a noble white knight

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.430
to hide his hateful nature.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:57.061
Aemond says that he and Criston are “decent
men with no taste for depravity”, which

00:13:57.061 --> 00:14:00.670
is nonsense, cause Criston killed a man just
this morning.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:04.970
He once beat a man to death at a wedding.

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:11.079
But the rules of honour and chivalry in this
world allow bad people to call themselves

00:14:11.079 --> 00:14:12.320
righteous.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:18.360
Alicent does the same thing, using her cloak
of righteousness to hide her jealousy and

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:19.360
hate.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:24.259
Aemond and Criston can’t find Aegon because
they don’t know where Aegon hangs out.

00:14:24.259 --> 00:14:29.190
But Ser Erryk is Aegon’s sworn protector,
his personal guard.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:34.200
So Erryk knows that Aegon often visits this..
child fighting pit.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:40.149
Here, children with sharp filed teeth fight
each other for entertainment.

00:14:40.149 --> 00:14:46.829
This is the deep dark underbelly of King’s
Landing, and Aegon participates in this evil.

00:14:46.829 --> 00:14:53.570
Aegon has a bastard child who he leaves here
in the pit, not exactly father of the year.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:58.380
Aegon’s a monster, and yet they’re making
him king.

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:03.889
Erryk says that Aegon is unfit to rule, they
shouldn’t support him as king.

00:15:03.889 --> 00:15:08.339
But his twin Arryk wants to keep his oath
and stay loyal to Aegon.

00:15:08.339 --> 00:15:15.370
A woman called Jeyne reveals that Mysaria
has Aegon, so Otto meets with Mysaria.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:20.730
Mysaria has worked with Otto before as a spymaster,
but this is the first time Otto’s met the

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.529
White Worm in person.

00:15:22.529 --> 00:15:26.730
Mysaria says she has Aegon hostage, and she
could kill him.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:32.899
She’ll release Aegon if Otto ends the use
of children in fighting pits.

00:15:32.899 --> 00:15:35.770
We know that Mysaria was once a slave.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:39.241
We see a scar on Mysaria’s neck, she has
suffered.

00:15:39.241 --> 00:15:45.040
So Mysaria sympathises with these exploited
children, and wants them freed.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:52.360
Or perhaps to use the kids in her child spy
network – seems hypocritical that she also

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.490
uses kids.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:59.510
But Otto says he’ll look into the fighting
pits, and Mysaria tells him where Aegon is.

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:06.829
Mysaria might not trust Otto to actually close
the fighting pits, Mysaria has been betrayed

00:16:06.829 --> 00:16:11.170
and let down before, this is more about sending
a message.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:15.000
Mysaria tells Otto that the common people
are powerful.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:20.540
And if Otto and King Aegon don’t treat the
people right, there will consequences.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:26.110
In Game of Thrones we see the power of the
people in riots and uprisings.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:29.390
Erryk and Arryk find Aegon in the sept.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:34.910
It’s ironic to find this drunk depraved
asshole in a holy sacred place.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:40.800
But before they can take Aegon to Otto, they’re
stopped by Criston and Aemond, who wanna take

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.480
Aegon to Alicent.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:48.070
Arryk fights Criston, but his brother Erryk
just watches and does nothing.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:54.550
Erryk doesn’t want to help crown the monstrous
Aegon, and he realises he can’t change Arryk’s

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.550
mind.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:59.279
So Erryk leaves to support Rhaenyra instead.

00:16:59.279 --> 00:17:05.250
This conflict is dividing families, even putting
these twins on opposite sides.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:09.790
Aegon tells Aemond to let him go, so Aegon
can flee the country.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:15.260
Aegon doesn’t want to be king, he says he’d
be a terrible king, and Aemond agrees.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:22.400
But Aegon is the eldest son, so his family
drags him kicking and screaming onto the Throne.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:26.190
So Alicent captures Aegon, she wins the game.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:30.160
And now that she holds the prince, she controls
the succession.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:34.400
She tells Otto they won’t kill Rhaenyra,
they’ll make Rhaenyra a good peace offer,

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:39.539
so Rhaenyra and her family can go into exile
in the east, like Daenerys and Viserys did

00:17:39.539 --> 00:17:41.049
in Game of Thrones.

00:17:41.049 --> 00:17:45.270
Alicent will make Criston the Commander of
the Kingsguard Commander to replace Harrold,

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:48.490
and they’ll crown Aegon King of Westeros.

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:52.140
The scene is shot to mirror a scene from Episode
1.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:57.720
Back then, Otto totally controlled Alicent
– he pushed her into marrying Viserys, and

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.770
made her the queen.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:04.540
But now, Alicent finally sees how much Otto
manipulated her for his goals.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:11.010
Now, after years of obedience Alicent finally
rebels against her father and takes charge

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:13.270
as her own power.

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:17.580
And Otto’s reaction is to say that Alicent
looks like her mother.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:24.820
It’s like in Episode 1, when he tells Alicent
to wear her mother’s dress to comfort Viserys.

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:30.980
Alicent is trying to assert herself as a political
equal here – but Otto makes it about her

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.820
appearance as a woman.

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:38.120
He also says that Alicent’s reluctance to
kill Rhaenyra is “squeamishness”, as though

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:42.130
Alicent is too delicate a lady to do a murder.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:47.789
He doesn’t understand that Alicent’s mercy
is a serious moral and political decision,

00:18:47.789 --> 00:18:49.799
not a weakness.

00:18:49.799 --> 00:18:54.909
Like Rhaenyra with Viserys, Alicent is frustrated
that her father still sees her just as his

00:18:54.909 --> 00:18:57.820
little girl, not as an equal.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:03.620
Larys finds out that Mysaria has spies in
the Red Keep – people like Talya and that

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.940
blonde kid telling Mysaria important secrets.

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:09.530
And Otto has been allowing this, so he can
benefit from the spying.

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:15.690
Alicent doesn’t trust Mysaria or Otto at
this point, so she asks Larys to kill Mysaria,

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:21.050
and Larys sends one of his fireflies to burn
Mysaria’s house.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:25.240
Last time Larys burned people, Alicent was
shocked and horrified.

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:29.880
But now, she’s asking Larys to murder people
for her.

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:33.580
Alicent is slowly embracing Larys’ evil.

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:36.720
And Larys might be manipulating Alicent.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:42.030
Earlier, he seemed to offer to spy on Alicent
for Otto.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.710
He’s playing both sides.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:49.570
And we still don’t know how Larys found
out about Rhaenyra’s moon tea.

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:53.640
Maybe Larys is actually working with Mysaria
and her spies.

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:59.580
We don’t see if Mysaria dies in that fire,
maybe Larys let her go.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.860
Larys’ true motivations are a mystery.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:06.660
But we do know one thing – he likes feet.

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:12.200
As payment for his services, Alicent shows
Larys her bare feet for him to masturbate

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.289
to.

00:20:13.289 --> 00:20:19.660
This seems to be an ongoing thing, Larys gives
secrets and does murders so Alicent shows

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:21.360
him feet.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:27.990
Since Larys has a deformed foot himself it
kinda makes sense that he’s into nice feet.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.940
And it’s not just about sex.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:37.169
Larys enjoys having power over people, making
them uncomfortable, like those prisoners previously.

00:20:37.169 --> 00:20:43.440
Maybe after a lifetime of being disrespected
for being disabled, Larys enjoys dominating

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:49.210
others, and humiliating the queen would be
the ultimate power trip.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:55.190
We get a nice brooding montage as the characters
contemplate their awful decisions.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.370
And Erryk frees Rhaenys.

00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:01.260
Erryk wants to help Rhaenyra’s side instead
of Aegon.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:05.559
So Erryk and Rhaenys escape through one of
the Keep’s secret passages.

00:21:05.559 --> 00:21:12.029
Rhaenys stares at the skull of Balerion – a
reminder of the power, danger and death they

00:21:12.029 --> 00:21:14.590
are risking in this conflict.

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:19.779
On the way out, Rhaenys is caught up in a
flood of people heading for the Dragonpit.

00:21:19.779 --> 00:21:26.630
The greens herd the common folk like sheep
toward the Dragonpit for Aegon’s coronation.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:32.900
Alicent takes Aegon to his coronation, and
Aegon says the truth – that Viserys obviously

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:37.679
didn’t want Aegon to be king, because Viserys
didn’t like Aegon.

00:21:37.679 --> 00:21:44.010
After Aegon stopped being a cute baby, Viserys
seemed to ignore his son – except to occasionally

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:49.309
shout at him – so of course Viserys didn’t
choose Aegon to be king – Aegon laughs at

00:21:49.309 --> 00:21:50.610
the absurdity of it.

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:55.760
Though as he laughs, he also feels the pain
of his father’s rejection.

00:21:55.760 --> 00:22:02.630
Aegon is a lot like Tyrion in the later books
– Tyrion also feels rejected and unloved,

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:06.559
and also does horrible things in the books.

00:22:06.559 --> 00:22:12.250
Alicent gives Aegon the Valyrian steel knife
that was once Aegon the Conqueror’s.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:17.720
This knife symbolises the huge responsibility
of the Throne, it represents the prophecy

00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:22.010
that the Targaryens must be united to defeat
the white walkers.

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:28.710
Aegon doesn’t even know about this prophecy,
he is not ready for this responsibility.

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:34.470
Alicent tells Aegon that as king, he should
not be cruel, and he should not kill Rhaenyra.

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:38.789
But Aegon doesn’t listen, Aegon never listened
to Alicent.

00:22:38.789 --> 00:22:43.360
He’s never cared about other peoples’
feelings, Aegon is a rapist who leaves his

00:22:43.360 --> 00:22:47.650
own children in fighting pits, he shouldn’t
be king.

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:53.460
But his mother Alicent blindly pushes him
into politics, just like Otto pushed Alicent

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:55.100
into politics.

00:22:55.100 --> 00:23:02.210
All Aegon wants is love – he asks Alicent
if she loves him, and she calls him an imbecile.

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:08.750
The Dragonpit is big open space, well fortified
against attack, so it’s where the greens

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:11.020
hold Aegon’s coronation.

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:16.620
This is where the royal kids had dragon lessons
previously – the Targaryen dragons are kept

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:18.890
in tunnels below.

00:23:18.890 --> 00:23:23.780
With much pomp and pageantry, Aegon comes
to claim his crown.

00:23:23.780 --> 00:23:30.200
The grandeur of the ceremony contrasts with
the ugly depravity that brought Aegon here.

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:35.390
Septon Eustace anoints Aegon with the seven
holy oils of the Faith of the Seven.

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:40.409
Septon Eustace is one of the main historical
sources in Fire &amp; Blood, alongside Mushroom

00:23:40.409 --> 00:23:41.630
and Orwyle.

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:45.240
Aegon wears the crown of Aegon the Conqueror.

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:50.330
Aegon’s crown is made of Valyrian steel
decorated with rubies.

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:55.059
Which is different to the crown worn by Viserys
and Jaehaerys before him.

00:23:55.059 --> 00:24:00.140
That crown is gold, decorated with sigils
of the houses of Westeros.

00:24:00.140 --> 00:24:03.150
It symbolises peace and unity.

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:06.750
While Aegon the Conqueror’s crown is more
warlike.

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:12.010
Aegon also wears the Conqueror’s knife,
and the Conqueror’s legendary Valyrian steel

00:24:12.010 --> 00:24:14.140
sword Blackfyre.

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:16.290
These are important symbols of legitimacy.

00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:22.540
Varys says that “Power resides where men
believe it resides”.

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:28.270
And men believe that whoever has the king’s
crown, and the sword, and is anointed by the

00:24:28.270 --> 00:24:33.700
septon, and has the name Aegon Targaryen and
blond hair, and is a firstborn son, and is

00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:37.490
in King’s Landing with the Iron Throne – that
man is the rightful king, as far as most people

00:24:37.490 --> 00:24:38.669
are concerned.

00:24:38.669 --> 00:24:41.660
When Aegon is crowned, he looks to his family.

00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:44.149
He gets a nod from Alicent.

00:24:44.149 --> 00:24:50.190
Helaena looks unhappy, she doesn’t wanna
be queen, and Aemond looks jealous cause he

00:24:50.190 --> 00:24:51.250
wants the throne.

00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:56.789
But then Aegon looks to the common folk – and
the people cheer for him, and Aegon loves

00:24:56.789 --> 00:24:57.789
it.

00:24:57.789 --> 00:25:04.470
Aegon feels rejected by his family, he’s
desperate for affection, and suddenly he gets

00:25:04.470 --> 00:25:10.010
a wave of love from people, it’s the validation
he’s always wanted.

00:25:10.010 --> 00:25:14.929
So all of a sudden, Aegon might decide he
wants to be king after all.

00:25:14.929 --> 00:25:19.640
Maybe the love of the people will change Aegon,
maybe he'll actually try to be a good king.

00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:24.399
Though there’s a similar scene in Game of
Thrones where Joffrey discovers the love of

00:25:24.399 --> 00:25:25.740
the common people.

00:25:25.740 --> 00:25:29.590
And that didn’t make Joffrey a good person.

00:25:29.590 --> 00:25:34.730
This moment of triumph for the greens is rudely
interrupted by a dragon.

00:25:34.730 --> 00:25:39.450
Rhaenys had sneaked down into the pit to get
her dragon Meleys.

00:25:39.450 --> 00:25:45.390
And she decides to escape by bursting up through
the floor of the Dragonpit, killing a lot

00:25:45.390 --> 00:25:47.190
of innocent common people.

00:25:47.190 --> 00:25:53.679
Rhaenys faces the greens, and she almost decides
to kill them all, to end their power grab.

00:25:53.679 --> 00:25:59.220
But Rhaenys looks into Alicent’s eyes, sees
her protecting her son Aegon.

00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:01.230
The greens are Rhaenys’ cousins.

00:26:01.230 --> 00:26:06.610
Does she really want to murder her extended
family, after Rhaenys has recently lost her

00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:09.409
own children, and her husband lies wounded?

00:26:09.409 --> 00:26:13.840
Alicent had told Rhaenys that she wants peace.

00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:16.700
So Rhaenys gives peace a chance.

00:26:16.700 --> 00:26:23.290
She lets the greens live, and flies off – stomping
several more common folk in the process.

00:26:23.290 --> 00:26:30.620
So Rhaenys shows mercy to the greens, but
massacres innocent people like it’s nothing.

00:26:30.620 --> 00:26:35.039
Many lords and ladies don’t much care about
the lives of peasants.

00:26:35.039 --> 00:26:40.080
When the lords play their game of thrones,
it’s always the innocent people who suffer.

00:26:40.080 --> 00:26:42.490
Especially when dragons are involved.

00:26:42.490 --> 00:26:47.200
Previously, we saw Daemon’s dragon stomp
on one of his own soldiers.

00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:50.750
In Game of Thrones, Daenerys’ dragons eat
children.

00:26:50.750 --> 00:26:56.210
Viserys said that dragons are a dangerous
uncontrollable power.

00:26:56.210 --> 00:27:00.870
And whenever the Targaryens use their dragons,
innocent people die.

00:27:00.870 --> 00:27:03.910
The Targaryens might not think that matters.

00:27:03.910 --> 00:27:07.750
But Mysaria warned us of the power of the
people.

00:27:07.750 --> 00:27:11.850
So Rhaenys’ mass murder may have consequences.

00:27:11.850 --> 00:27:19.480
Aegon’s coronation fulfils Viserys’ prophecy
about his son being king, wearing Aegon’s

00:27:19.480 --> 00:27:20.480
crown.

00:27:20.480 --> 00:27:25.570
And Meleys bursting up through the floor fulfils
Helaena’s prophecy about a beast beneath

00:27:25.570 --> 00:27:27.070
the boards.

00:27:27.070 --> 00:27:29.940
But there are deeper meanings.

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:35.149
Like the beastly Aegon is found beneath an
altar in a sept.

00:27:35.149 --> 00:27:41.460
Beneath the grand ceremony of the coronation
is the political corruption of the greens.

00:27:41.460 --> 00:27:47.669
Beneath the power of the Targaryen dragons
are hidden beasts – Mysaria and Larys are

00:27:47.669 --> 00:27:54.080
symbolised by worms and fireflies, spiders
and bees and wasps are also mentioned this

00:27:54.080 --> 00:27:55.330
episode.

00:27:55.330 --> 00:28:01.779
With their hidden passages and deadly secrets,
they too are beasts beneath the boards.

00:28:01.779 --> 00:28:06.380
Daemon said that everyone is capable of depravity.

00:28:06.380 --> 00:28:12.090
We’ve seen the violence beneath Alicent’s
courtesy, beneath Criston’s chivalry, beneath

00:28:12.090 --> 00:28:14.480
Otto’s cold politics.

00:28:14.480 --> 00:28:20.539
As this conflict gets worse, what other beasts
will emerge from below?

00:28:20.539 --> 00:28:25.830
If you wanna know the full story of Hot D,
you’ve gotta check out the book, Fire &amp; Blood.

00:28:25.830 --> 00:28:30.929
There’s also the main series of Game of
Thrones books, and the worldbook, and Dunk

00:28:30.929 --> 00:28:31.929
